      "content": "Scientists generally advocate for mandatory vaccination based on the **herd immunity principle and the public good of disease control**, arguing that high uptake is necessary to protect the most vulnerable in the community.\n\nIn contrast, civil liberties advocates frequently argue against mandates, focusing on **bodily autonomy and the right to make personal medical decisions** without government coercion.\n\nThis debate often centers on the conflict between collective public health benefit and individual rights to choose one's own medical care.",
